1
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:58,008
We'll be right back.

2
00:00:58,028 --> 00:01:28,008
We'll be right back.

3
00:01:28,028 --> 00:01:58,008
We'll be right back.

4
00:01:59,028 --> 00:02:00,508
Superior, huh?

5
00:02:02,068 --> 00:02:03,768
All right, Chief. Go ahead.

6
00:02:04,128 --> 00:02:06,448
Hot, hot! Ouch, ouch, ouch!

7
00:02:06,748 --> 00:02:08,448
I spilled coffee all over myself!

8
00:02:08,808 --> 00:02:09,228
Damn it!

9
00:02:10,008 --> 00:02:11,008
Stupid coffee!

10
00:02:11,008 --> 00:02:13,528
What the heck?

11
00:02:14,368 --> 00:02:16,088
So, you're still alive.

12
00:02:16,528 --> 00:02:18,448
Greetings, Cutty Flam.

13
00:02:19,488 --> 00:02:21,408
Long time no see.

14
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:25,768
It's hard to believe you somehow managed to survive the accident.

15
00:02:26,948 --> 00:02:28,208
Hard to believe.

16
00:02:28,928 --> 00:02:30,308
But good news nonetheless.

17
00:02:31,768 --> 00:02:32,568
Is that so?

18
00:02:32,948 --> 00:02:33,828
Who are you?

19
00:02:34,588 --> 00:02:36,248
Don't you remember me?

20
00:02:38,488 --> 00:02:41,408
I'm the man from Cypher Pool number five

21
00:02:41,408 --> 00:02:44,568
that arrested Tom's workers when I caught them red-handed

22
00:02:44,568 --> 00:02:47,888
for savagely attacking the judicial ship eight years ago.

23
00:02:47,888 --> 00:02:52,648
You're that Sponda guy, aren't you?

24
00:02:52,708 --> 00:02:53,508
Spondam!

25
00:02:53,668 --> 00:02:54,788
You're missing the M!

26
00:02:56,348 --> 00:02:59,168
But I'll have plenty of time to drill that into your head

27
00:02:59,168 --> 00:03:00,728
once you arrive at Eni's lobby.

28
00:03:01,308 --> 00:03:02,588
Make it quick, Ben.

29
00:03:02,588 --> 00:03:05,548
I'm simply dying to teach that criminal a lesson.

30
00:03:07,048 --> 00:03:07,308
Huh?

31
00:03:11,868 --> 00:03:13,528
Damn stupid lamp!

32
00:03:14,468 --> 00:03:15,468
Tie him up.

33
00:03:17,308 --> 00:03:18,028
Ow!

34
00:03:19,648 --> 00:03:20,808
Hey, punk!

35
00:03:20,988 --> 00:03:22,188
Watch those hands!

36
00:03:22,628 --> 00:03:23,068
Come on.

37
00:03:32,588 --> 00:03:37,028
Let him go!

38
00:03:38,128 --> 00:03:39,788
Come back here, you bastards!

39
00:03:46,068 --> 00:03:46,808
I'm sorry.

40
00:03:47,608 --> 00:03:48,048
Hey!

41
00:03:48,188 --> 00:03:50,668
If you're not gonna help, then don't get my hoops up!

42
00:03:52,448 --> 00:03:53,968
Wait, I know you, don't I?

43
00:03:54,188 --> 00:03:55,608
You're part of the Straw Hat crew.

44
00:03:57,368 --> 00:03:57,848
Huh?

45
00:04:02,588 --> 00:04:30,848
Don't any of the

46
00:04:30,848 --> 00:04:43,988
The Truth Behind Her Betrayal, Robin's Sorrowful Decision.

47
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:52,608
Last train of the day is cutting it kind of close.

48
00:04:53,088 --> 00:04:54,868
Wonder what the government's got in mind.

49
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:58,628
Dunno, but it must be serious if they're going out during Aqua Lacuna.

50
00:04:58,908 --> 00:05:00,388
Yeah, that sounds about right.

51
00:05:00,848 --> 00:05:03,748
I heard the people getting on tonight are big-shot secret agents.

52
00:05:04,048 --> 00:05:04,968
That's news to me.

53
00:05:05,228 --> 00:05:08,388
Some folks from the Navy were talking about it just a few minutes ago.

54
00:05:09,008 --> 00:05:14,108
From what I gather, the government sent this team of undercover agents to Water 7 a bunch of years ago,

55
00:05:14,168 --> 00:05:15,748
and they just now finished their mission.

56
00:05:16,428 --> 00:05:17,108
Nice timing.

57
00:05:17,288 --> 00:05:18,068
No kidding.

58
00:05:18,368 --> 00:05:19,788
Course I didn't hear the details.

59
00:05:20,108 --> 00:05:21,888
Who knows what they were doing all these years?

60
00:05:24,048 --> 00:05:26,808
And you said these guys were undercover now, didn't you?

61
00:05:26,808 --> 00:05:29,028
That means they might be people we already know.

62
00:05:30,848 --> 00:05:34,488
Actually, you're right.

63
00:05:34,708 --> 00:05:35,588
Now keep this a secret.

64
00:05:36,008 --> 00:05:38,328
But I think I might have a good idea who they are.

65
00:05:38,748 --> 00:05:39,108
Who?

66
00:05:39,708 --> 00:05:40,348
Tell me.

67
00:05:45,748 --> 00:05:46,268
What?

68
00:05:46,448 --> 00:05:47,408
From the back streets?

69
00:05:47,728 --> 00:05:48,388
Mm-hmm.

70
00:05:48,388 --> 00:05:53,948
I've caught them having some real hush-hush conversations in the corner over at Blue Nose Bar.

71
00:05:54,588 --> 00:05:57,928
That might be a little fishy, but I don't think it means they're secret agents.

72
00:05:58,028 --> 00:05:59,088
It's not just that.

73
00:05:59,488 --> 00:06:03,488
They're always spending money and living like kings, even though they hardly work at all.

74
00:06:03,628 --> 00:06:04,708
That's a good point.

75
00:06:04,708 --> 00:06:07,868
I've seen them ride first class quite a few times.

76
00:06:07,988 --> 00:06:08,408
See?

77
00:06:09,128 --> 00:06:13,468
Well, whether I'm right or not, we'll find out their secret identity soon enough.

78
00:06:13,848 --> 00:06:16,508
After all, they'll be boarding the sea train any minute now.

79
00:06:16,908 --> 00:06:19,708
Mark my words, this will be the talk of the whole town tomorrow.

80
00:06:20,048 --> 00:06:21,028
I'm sure.

81
00:06:21,028 --> 00:06:51,008
Mark my words, this will be the talk of the whole town tomorrow.

82
00:06:51,008 --> 00:06:52,168
Oh, yeah.

83
00:06:52,548 --> 00:06:53,148
Iceberg.

84
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:54,208
Pauly.

85
00:07:03,588 --> 00:07:04,388
Nami.

86
00:07:05,048 --> 00:07:05,668
Oh, no.

87
00:07:06,408 --> 00:07:08,568
I have to treat her right away.

88
00:07:09,428 --> 00:07:11,368
If I can just...

89
00:07:11,368 --> 00:07:11,468
Oh.

90
00:07:21,008 --> 00:07:22,908
Hurry!

91
00:07:23,208 --> 00:07:24,068
They need first aid.

92
00:07:24,148 --> 00:07:25,028
They're burned all over.

93
00:07:25,168 --> 00:07:26,728
Hey, what are we going to do with this reindeer?

94
00:07:27,148 --> 00:07:27,608
Help him.

95
00:07:27,808 --> 00:07:29,068
He's saying they're lies.

96
00:07:29,328 --> 00:07:30,068
You're right.

97
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:31,668
Hey, someone give me a hand.

98
00:07:31,668 --> 00:07:36,168
Oh, boy.

99
00:07:36,168 --> 00:07:42,708
That's just sad.

100
00:07:46,708 --> 00:07:51,988
So what you're saying is that you left the straw hats, but you haven't given up your life of crime.

101
00:07:52,448 --> 00:07:53,408
What a shame.

102
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:56,648
If you're a pirate, you're coming with us.

103
00:07:57,028 --> 00:07:57,368
Khalifa?

104
00:07:57,808 --> 00:07:58,448
Got it.

105
00:07:58,448 --> 00:08:07,448
And as for this ship, you still haven't disposed of it?

106
00:08:07,828 --> 00:08:08,588
Stay away!

107
00:08:08,888 --> 00:08:10,288
Don't you dare touch her!

108
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:22,268
Are you listening to me?

109
00:08:22,408 --> 00:08:23,328
What are you doing?

110
00:08:23,328 --> 00:08:29,988
Even if it was only a temporary disguise, we are still respected as shipwrights.

111
00:08:35,448 --> 00:08:39,488
When we say your ship's done for, then you would do well to listen to us.

112
00:08:40,868 --> 00:08:42,048
What do you care?

113
00:08:42,248 --> 00:08:43,448
It's not even your ship.

114
00:08:43,588 --> 00:08:45,208
I can do whatever I want with it.

115
00:08:45,548 --> 00:08:47,648
This lever releases the water, right?

116
00:08:48,148 --> 00:08:48,988
Cut it out.

117
00:08:49,188 --> 00:08:50,508
That's not funny, damn it.

118
00:08:50,948 --> 00:08:51,368
Hey!

119
00:08:53,328 --> 00:09:04,508
No, stop it!

120
00:09:05,268 --> 00:09:06,588
Don't let her fall!

121
00:09:19,908 --> 00:09:20,748
Don't worry.

122
00:09:20,748 --> 00:09:24,548
I'll carry everyone for a little bit longer.

123
00:09:41,828 --> 00:09:42,428
Mary!

124
00:09:42,428 --> 00:09:54,968
Get back!

125
00:09:54,968 --> 00:09:56,048
I'll cover me!

126
00:09:56,048 --> 00:09:56,648
I'll cover me!

127
00:09:56,648 --> 00:09:58,108
I'll cover!

128
00:09:58,108 --> 00:10:01,188
You idiot, run!

129
00:10:07,188 --> 00:10:07,848
Dammit!

130
00:10:07,848 --> 00:10:09,688
Is there anything we can do?

131
00:10:20,888 --> 00:10:21,408
Look!

132
00:10:21,668 --> 00:10:23,028
Mr. Iceberg's awake!

133
00:10:25,028 --> 00:10:25,828
All right!

134
00:10:25,968 --> 00:10:26,668
He's safe!

135
00:10:26,768 --> 00:10:27,868
I knew he'd make it!

136
00:10:28,328 --> 00:10:28,668
Hey!

137
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:29,828
Go, go!

138
00:10:30,068 --> 00:10:30,368
Ah!

139
00:10:31,028 --> 00:10:32,968
That reindeer saved his life!

140
00:10:32,968 --> 00:10:33,728
Are you sure?

141
00:10:34,028 --> 00:10:36,008
I thought it belonged to the Straw Hats!

142
00:10:40,808 --> 00:10:41,228
Hey!

143
00:10:41,428 --> 00:10:41,848
Look!

144
00:10:42,228 --> 00:10:44,268
This woman's from the Straw Hats, too!

145
00:10:46,988 --> 00:10:48,588
So, what now?

146
00:10:48,928 --> 00:10:51,168
Do you think maybe we should tie her up and question her?

147
00:10:51,388 --> 00:10:52,028
I don't know.

148
00:10:52,128 --> 00:10:53,028
She's just a girl.

149
00:10:53,208 --> 00:10:54,248
And she's hurt, too.

150
00:10:54,248 --> 00:10:55,748
I know, but...

151
00:10:55,748 --> 00:10:57,288
Whoa!

152
00:10:57,468 --> 00:10:59,128
You shouldn't be moving yet, Mr. Iceberg!

153
00:11:06,588 --> 00:11:07,388
Sorry, men.

154
00:11:07,908 --> 00:11:09,728
But I need a little space right now.

155
00:11:10,448 --> 00:11:11,288
That is to say,

156
00:11:11,428 --> 00:11:13,308
I want to speak to this woman in private.

157
00:11:14,308 --> 00:11:14,628
Huh?

158
00:11:14,628 --> 00:11:43,468
I wonder what those two are talking about.

159
00:11:43,468 --> 00:11:44,388
Beats me!

160
00:11:45,448 --> 00:11:47,748
What was that for?

161
00:11:47,848 --> 00:11:48,948
Stop standing, man!

162
00:11:49,028 --> 00:11:49,888
Give me a hand!

163
00:11:50,008 --> 00:11:51,688
I know Iceberg and Polly are safe,

164
00:11:51,808 --> 00:11:54,228
but the rest of the foreman might still be trapped inside!

165
00:11:54,648 --> 00:11:55,668
Yeah, he's right.

166
00:11:55,908 --> 00:11:56,388
Let's go!

167
00:11:56,748 --> 00:11:57,668
Oh, but...

168
00:11:57,668 --> 00:11:58,488
Yeah, sorry!

169
00:12:01,368 --> 00:12:02,368
Well...

170
00:12:02,368 --> 00:12:03,708
First off,

171
00:12:03,968 --> 00:12:05,248
I must apologize.

172
00:12:05,928 --> 00:12:08,548
I falsely accused your entire crew.

173
00:12:09,328 --> 00:12:10,868
I'll try to clear that up soon.

174
00:12:11,988 --> 00:12:12,908
But for now,

175
00:12:12,908 --> 00:12:15,228
I want to talk about Nico Robin.

176
00:12:16,228 --> 00:12:17,228
What do you know?

177
00:12:17,228 --> 00:12:20,408
When you first came to Water 7,

178
00:12:20,488 --> 00:12:21,868
did she start acting strangely?

179
00:12:22,288 --> 00:12:23,628
Yeah, she did.

180
00:12:24,288 --> 00:12:25,788
She went into town that day

181
00:12:25,788 --> 00:12:26,988
and then never came back.

182
00:12:27,228 --> 00:12:28,128
But the next morning,

183
00:12:28,808 --> 00:12:30,768
she was the prime suspect

184
00:12:30,768 --> 00:12:31,928
in your attempted murder.

185
00:12:31,928 --> 00:12:35,188
When Sanji and Chopper finally saw her again,

186
00:12:36,188 --> 00:12:37,448
she said this was goodbye

187
00:12:37,448 --> 00:12:39,228
and wouldn't be a part of the crew anymore.

188
00:12:39,988 --> 00:12:42,168
Of course, none of that made any sense to us,

189
00:12:42,248 --> 00:12:44,468
so we decided to break into your mansion

190
00:12:44,468 --> 00:12:46,828
in hopes that we'd be able to see her one more time

191
00:12:46,828 --> 00:12:47,908
and find out the truth.

192
00:12:47,908 --> 00:12:51,468
I did it to make my wish come true.

193
00:12:52,148 --> 00:12:54,368
One that can't happen as long as we're together.

194
00:12:54,548 --> 00:12:56,008
If you can't accept that, I'm sorry.

195
00:12:58,228 --> 00:12:59,888
What kind of wish would force her

196
00:12:59,888 --> 00:13:01,228
to give up all of her friends?

197
00:13:01,228 --> 00:13:05,168
I think I know the answer, actually.

198
00:13:09,408 --> 00:13:11,128
This probably started shortly

199
00:13:11,128 --> 00:13:13,208
after you lost sight of her for the first time.

200
00:13:16,228 --> 00:13:16,748
CP9.

201
00:13:17,308 --> 00:13:19,148
The government had begun its operation

202
00:13:19,148 --> 00:13:20,468
the moment she arrived.

203
00:13:20,468 --> 00:13:24,248
In other words,

204
00:13:24,288 --> 00:13:25,068
there's a good reason

205
00:13:25,068 --> 00:13:26,768
why your friend did what she did.

206
00:13:27,588 --> 00:13:29,388
But before I go into the details,

207
00:13:29,508 --> 00:13:30,448
I want you to understand

208
00:13:30,448 --> 00:13:32,028
that both Nico Robin and I

209
00:13:32,028 --> 00:13:34,028
have the means to revive an ancient weapon

210
00:13:34,028 --> 00:13:36,828
that is capable of destroying the entire world.

211
00:13:37,828 --> 00:13:38,708
A weapon?

212
00:13:39,188 --> 00:13:39,888
That's right.

213
00:13:43,888 --> 00:13:44,628
It's me.

214
00:13:45,068 --> 00:13:46,568
We've hit a snag in the plan.

215
00:13:47,788 --> 00:13:49,648
Everyone head to the bedroom immediately.

216
00:13:50,468 --> 00:13:52,568
Don't shoot Iceberg yet.

217
00:13:54,508 --> 00:13:56,508
Do you understand now?

218
00:13:56,888 --> 00:13:58,448
The blueprints that they found

219
00:13:58,448 --> 00:13:59,868
are fake.

220
00:14:02,188 --> 00:14:03,288
I don't care.

221
00:14:03,788 --> 00:14:04,948
I would rather die

222
00:14:04,948 --> 00:14:06,148
than hand over that information

223
00:14:06,148 --> 00:14:06,908
to the government.

224
00:14:07,628 --> 00:14:08,928
But now it's not that simple.

225
00:14:09,368 --> 00:14:10,148
If you've decided

226
00:14:10,148 --> 00:14:11,248
that you're going to help them

227
00:14:11,248 --> 00:14:12,228
and you're searching

228
00:14:12,228 --> 00:14:13,588
for the Ponyglyphs yourself,

229
00:14:13,908 --> 00:14:15,428
then I have to do everything

230
00:14:15,428 --> 00:14:16,688
I can to stop you.

231
00:14:18,008 --> 00:14:19,868
I understand your concern,

232
00:14:19,868 --> 00:14:21,648
but I'm only studying the Ponyglyphs

233
00:14:21,648 --> 00:14:23,528
to learn more about the history of the world.

234
00:14:23,908 --> 00:14:25,828
I don't care about the weapon.

235
00:14:25,828 --> 00:14:28,788
You have to take responsibility.

236
00:14:31,208 --> 00:14:33,268
I told you this would happen,

237
00:14:33,808 --> 00:14:35,708
but you don't listen.

238
00:14:36,748 --> 00:14:37,168
Frankie,

239
00:14:37,688 --> 00:14:39,668
even if you weren't trying to,

240
00:14:40,348 --> 00:14:42,668
weapons are made to hurt people.

241
00:14:43,348 --> 00:14:45,488
Whether you want them to or not,

242
00:14:45,568 --> 00:14:47,148
they can hurt your friends.

243
00:14:47,148 --> 00:14:50,608
Even if you don't have malicious intent,

244
00:14:50,928 --> 00:14:52,848
your actions can still hurt people.

245
00:14:53,268 --> 00:14:54,908
If your curiosity for history

246
00:14:54,908 --> 00:14:56,608
leads to the destruction of the world,

247
00:14:57,028 --> 00:14:58,448
then you're better off dying

248
00:14:58,448 --> 00:14:59,908
right here and right now,

249
00:15:00,008 --> 00:15:00,608
Nico Robin.

250
00:15:02,608 --> 00:15:04,208
Even after seeing what happened

251
00:15:04,208 --> 00:15:05,288
to the devils of Ohara,

252
00:15:05,628 --> 00:15:07,508
you still want to walk this path?

253
00:15:08,608 --> 00:15:11,108
You don't know a damn thing about Ohara!

254
00:15:11,108 --> 00:15:16,428
You have no idea

255
00:15:16,428 --> 00:15:17,628
how much the world government

256
00:15:17,628 --> 00:15:18,768
has warped my life.

257
00:15:19,068 --> 00:15:19,968
Do you hear me?

258
00:15:23,068 --> 00:15:25,168
If you hate the government so much,

259
00:15:25,488 --> 00:15:26,748
then why help them?

260
00:15:32,568 --> 00:15:33,888
Because I have a wish

261
00:15:33,888 --> 00:15:35,768
that I would sacrifice anything for.

262
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:43,928
When I came to this town,

263
00:15:44,708 --> 00:15:46,688
CP-9 presented me with two conditions.

264
00:15:47,568 --> 00:15:49,288
The first was to pin your assassination

265
00:15:49,288 --> 00:15:50,468
on the Straw Hats

266
00:15:50,468 --> 00:15:51,908
and leave their crew.

267
00:15:52,948 --> 00:15:55,128
The second was to turn myself

268
00:15:55,128 --> 00:15:56,088
over to the government

269
00:15:56,088 --> 00:15:57,828
and follow their every order

270
00:15:57,828 --> 00:15:58,648
without question.

271
00:15:59,348 --> 00:16:01,468
You realize they won't let you live.

272
00:16:02,148 --> 00:16:03,908
You escaped them for 20 years.

273
00:16:04,308 --> 00:16:05,168
Why would you agree

274
00:16:05,168 --> 00:16:06,428
to something like that now?

275
00:16:08,108 --> 00:16:09,648
In this particular instance,

276
00:16:10,528 --> 00:16:12,308
CP-9 has been given permission

277
00:16:12,308 --> 00:16:14,048
to activate a buster call

278
00:16:14,048 --> 00:16:15,308
against the Straw Hats.

279
00:16:15,648 --> 00:16:16,788
A buster call?

280
00:16:17,548 --> 00:16:19,148
It's an emergency order

281
00:16:19,148 --> 00:16:21,208
that summons five vice admirals

282
00:16:21,208 --> 00:16:22,228
and ten battleships

283
00:16:22,228 --> 00:16:23,388
to the same location.

284
00:16:25,148 --> 00:16:27,088
No matter how strong you are,

285
00:16:27,588 --> 00:16:28,788
no one can survive

286
00:16:28,788 --> 00:16:30,448
a full-scale military attack

287
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:31,208
of that caliber.

288
00:16:32,608 --> 00:16:33,988
Under normal circumstances,

289
00:16:33,988 --> 00:16:35,568
only the three admirals

290
00:16:35,568 --> 00:16:36,548
and the head of the Navy,

291
00:16:36,748 --> 00:16:37,508
the fleet admiral,

292
00:16:37,688 --> 00:16:38,708
are allowed to exercise

293
00:16:38,708 --> 00:16:40,008
that kind of authority.

294
00:16:40,948 --> 00:16:41,248
However,

295
00:16:41,728 --> 00:16:43,168
this is a special case.

296
00:16:43,988 --> 00:16:44,968
Just this once,

297
00:16:45,548 --> 00:16:46,368
Admiral Aokiji

298
00:16:46,368 --> 00:16:47,868
has given CP-9

299
00:16:47,868 --> 00:16:49,248
the right to make the call.

300
00:16:49,928 --> 00:16:50,988
When I heard his name,

301
00:16:51,148 --> 00:16:51,648
I surrendered.

302
00:16:52,168 --> 00:16:52,908
If I hadn't agreed

303
00:16:52,908 --> 00:16:53,748
to their conditions,

304
00:16:53,868 --> 00:16:54,888
then me and the rest

305
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:55,648
of the Straw Hats

306
00:16:55,648 --> 00:16:56,668
would have been annihilated.

307
00:16:57,348 --> 00:16:58,748
For the past 20 years,

308
00:16:58,948 --> 00:17:00,328
I've been able to run away

309
00:17:00,328 --> 00:17:00,988
and survive,

310
00:17:01,088 --> 00:17:02,248
no matter what the circumstance.

311
00:17:02,248 --> 00:17:03,948
But that's only because

312
00:17:03,948 --> 00:17:05,488
I had nothing to protect.

313
00:17:06,068 --> 00:17:07,048
Because I was willing

314
00:17:07,048 --> 00:17:08,028
to betray others

315
00:17:08,028 --> 00:17:09,288
and use them as a shield.

316
00:17:09,708 --> 00:17:10,648
But not now.

317
00:17:11,248 --> 00:17:12,228
For the first time

318
00:17:12,228 --> 00:17:13,208
in all these years,

319
00:17:13,368 --> 00:17:14,428
I can't do that.

320
00:17:16,828 --> 00:17:18,048
They picked up

321
00:17:18,048 --> 00:17:19,388
the life I gave up on,

322
00:17:20,268 --> 00:17:21,748
returned the heart I lost,

323
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:24,228
and continued the dreams

324
00:17:24,228 --> 00:17:25,808
that I no longer believed in.

325
00:17:25,808 --> 00:17:28,708
Even after all I've done,

326
00:17:29,768 --> 00:17:30,728
I've found friends

327
00:17:30,728 --> 00:17:32,508
who will still believe in me.

328
00:17:33,468 --> 00:17:34,168
I see.

329
00:17:34,828 --> 00:17:36,248
But then what is your wish?

330
00:17:39,248 --> 00:17:40,568
That excluding me,

331
00:17:40,828 --> 00:17:42,608
all of the other Straw Hat Pirates

332
00:17:42,608 --> 00:17:43,168
will be allowed

333
00:17:43,168 --> 00:17:44,588
to leave this island safely!

334
00:17:47,188 --> 00:17:48,848
And as long as you have that,

335
00:17:49,388 --> 00:17:50,688
you don't care what happens

336
00:17:50,688 --> 00:17:51,808
to the rest of the world?

337
00:17:51,808 --> 00:17:53,908
I don't!

338
00:21:55,180 --> 00:22:12,180
夢見た僕らは間違いじゃないと信じて 荒く埋れる海原を渡って行ける

339
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:22,180
誰よりも勇敢で思いやりもあるけれど

340
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:32,180
もしも君がこの船を降りて 違う世界にいたとしても

341
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:40,180
最後にはきっと笑えるよ

342
00:22:52,180 --> 00:23:00,380
luffyとZoroをお自らに 今回避けるとすわ

343
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:08,180
それはetinose5のusi6は1に脱付したイディストにして アンダーをごめんなさい

344
00:23:08,180 --> 00:23:10,420
The steam whistle forces friends apart.

345
00:23:10,740 --> 00:23:12,380
The sea train starts to run.

346
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:14,460
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

